hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1354","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abdul-Ala told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He led them with the prayer of fear, and he prayed one rak’ah in a group behind him, and a group facing the enemy, then the group who They prayed and faced the enemy, and the others came and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led one rak’ah with them, then he gave the salutation, then these people prayed one rak’ah and this one another rak’ah.”"
"1355","Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Yazid bin Zurayi narrated to us, Muammar narrated to us, something like it."
